  "gate_definitions": "Pre-registered gates (specification 24.2). Thresholds come from config['pilot']; nothing here is tuned to a result. 1. distribution: the P01 predeclared checks pass on all 80 calibration traces. 2. solo_feasibility: in each configuration, pooled over its calibration tasks, at least `solo_feasible_fraction` of tasks have a destination that meets the soft deadline when alone in an idle system. 3. heavy_pressure: for at least one (configuration, reference policy), the heavy workload shows a mean failure fraction above `heavy_failure_fraction_gt` while mean reliability stays above `heavy_reliability_gt`. A failure fraction above 1% is the measured symptom of resource pressure; the descriptive indicators are reported alongside. 4. complete: every planned episode is present, so a gate cannot pass on a partial run."
